<mxCell id="d6c31" value="Why √n is enough" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="214" width="400" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="d6c32" value="If n = a · b with a ≤ b, then a · a ≤ a · b = n, so a ≤ √n. Any composite n has a factor at or below √n, so checking beyond it finds nothing new." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="252" width="400" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
