<mxCell id="d14c51" value="&lt;b&gt;Time&lt;/b&gt;: N! leaves, and each permutation costs O(N) to build, so about N · N! work. Interviews drop the polynomial factor and call it the &lt;b&gt;N!&lt;/b&gt; class." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="484" width="480" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="d14c52" value="&lt;b&gt;Space&lt;/b&gt;: the recursion is only N deep, but every level keeps its own &lt;b&gt;rest&lt;/b&gt; slice (N − 1, N − 2, … letters), so extra space is about N²/2: &lt;b&gt;O(N²)&lt;/b&gt; besides the N! output lists." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="554" width="480" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="d14c53" value="&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; N! leaves; time in the Θ(N!) class (≈ N · N! work, polynomial factor dropped); O(N²) extra space for the rest slices on the stack, besides the output." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=13;align=left;spacingLeft=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="658" width="820" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
